  "limitations": [
    "Trained on simulated tissue only. No wet-lab perturbation data was used at any point.",
    "The cell-class vocabulary is fixed to the five types the generator produces. A dataset with other cell types maps them to the unknown-class slot.",
    "The feature space is the 66-node curated network. A dataset measuring other genes cannot be predicted on without a new pack.",
    "Stage indices count rounds of intercellular signalling in the model and are not calibrated to biological time (§7.8).",
    "On the cells one hop from a perturbed cell — where a spatial model has to earn its keep — this pack explains 10.5% of the variance (first-neighbour R² 0.105, Pearson 0.325). It is directional evidence about where a perturbation travels, not a quantitative prediction of how much any individual cell changes.",
    "Permuting the graph while keeping every cell's degree (the gnn-shuffled control) retains 88% of the first-neighbour R² (0.093 against 0.105). Most of what this model does is aggregate over *a* neighbourhood; the specific edges account for the remaining 12%. Read a propagation map as neighbourhood context first and edge-specific routing second.",
    "The ensemble interval is too narrow: 83.5% of held-out errors fell inside the nominal 90% interval. Treat the spread as a ranking of which predictions are less certain, not as a 90% interval. The correction factor is reported above and deliberately not applied."
  ]
